STATUS: PARTIAL — the login endpoint and successful session result were verified with Django's request client. The cURL command below is ready to run against a local server, but this execution sandbox prevents separate cURL processes from reaching the server's loopback listener. No real password, cookie, or CSRF token is saved here.

Verified route and request:
POST /djangoapp/login
Content-Type: application/json
JSON fields: username, password
Requires a CSRF token from GET /djangoapp/csrf and the corresponding session cookie.

Bash / Git Bash cURL command (use a valid account already registered in this app; set credentials in the environment, not in this file):
~~~bash
export BASE_URL='http://127.0.0.1:8000'
export APP_TEST_USERNAME='your_valid_username'
export APP_TEST_PASSWORD='your_valid_password'
COOKIE_JAR="$(mktemp)"
CSRF_JSON="$(curl -fsS -c "$COOKIE_JAR" "$BASE_URL/djangoapp/csrf")"
CSRF_TOKEN="$(printf '%s' "$CSRF_JSON" | python -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['csrfToken'])")"

curl -sS -b "$COOKIE_JAR" -c "$COOKIE_JAR" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H "X-CSRFToken: $CSRF_TOKEN" \
  --data "{\"username\":\"$APP_TEST_USERNAME\",\"password\":\"$APP_TEST_PASSWORD\"}" \
  -w '\nHTTP_STATUS=%{http_code}\n' \
  "$BASE_URL/djangoapp/login"

curl -sS -b "$COOKIE_JAR" -w '\nHTTP_STATUS=%{http_code}\n' \
  "$BASE_URL/djangoapp/session"
rm -f "$COOKIE_JAR"
~~~

